# Angular Framework Standards

## Component Architecture
- Use functional components with dependency injection
- Keep constructor parameters with same key-value naming: `private loggerService: LoggerService`
- Use `private` instead of `public` appropriately, avoid unnecessary `protected`
- Each component must have main container class matching filename

## Lifecycle Management
- Always unsubscribe in `ngOnDestroy` if using `subscribe()`
- Import and implement `OnDestroy` interface when needed
- Use `takeUntil(destroy$)` pattern for multiple subscriptions

## Dependency Injection
- Follow constructor parameter naming: `private userService: UserService`
- Use appropriate access modifiers (`private`, `public`, `protected`)
- Avoid circular dependencies

## Observable Pattern
```typescript
// Always unsubscribe pattern
private destroy$ = new Subject<void>();

ngOnInit() {
  this.dataService.getData()
    .pipe(takeUntil(this.destroy$))
    .subscribe(data => {
      // Handle data
    });
}

ngOnDestroy() {
  this.destroy$.next();
  this.destroy$.complete();
}
```

## Form Handling
- Use reactive forms over template-driven forms
- Implement proper form validation
- Add translation support for form labels and error messages